{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791557190,"nonce":"yhfz69dUaDQ2YDDYsih9StChhPI=","message":"Completed in 1aa6a51. ASHUI_HIT_MAP=1 enables the hit-map view in native windows and offscreen renders. The sampled native map colors topmost targets, including noninteractive containers, text and component roots; the exact pointer panel shows target/ancestor order, CSS tag/id, full native id, registered handlers, input-state ownership and focus/disabled flags. Amber shows the native region available for quiet hit caching. The docs distinguish native hit targets from bubbling event.target and actual handler propagation.\n\nUses the existing FrameOverlay and MotionOverlay drawing helpers in a separate tree, without creating source interactions or installing a ticker/pointer hook. Maps cache by hit revision and viewport, reuse native hit regions between samples, merge horizontal/vertical tiles, and cap work at 65,536 sample points. The requested/default grid spacing is labelled; exact pointer inspection is independent of sampling.\n\nVerification: 13 native-backed checks cover plain nodes/no handlers, overlapping paint order, native pass-through, clipped corners, every grid sample versus exact hits, caching/invalidation, viewport edges, work bounds, consumed pointer positions, isolation and disposal. The pure-HXX HitMap scene was captured with the existing snapshot runner and inspected at .ashui/snapshots/hit-map.png. Interactions, Demo and TreeMotion bytecode was rebuilt in demo/snapshot bins; native libraries remain current. With the debugger enabled, the Interactions native check routed 200 macOS mouse events to the process and observed zero Haxe UI ticks during quiet motion, then verified the correct retained coordinate at the next application wake. Logs are in ignored .ashui/hit-cache, including hit-map-test.log and quiet-hit-map.log. The native OS event pump still handles motion; it does not return quiet motion to the UI VM.\n\nUsage and semantics: docs/debugging.md; sample scene: tools/snapshot/scenes/HitMap.hx. Unrelated snapshots/ and tests/dump/ remain untouched.","files":null}]}